{"vid":"CcTui5xsUQg","source":"CcTui5xsUQg.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":2.9,"txt":"[MARIA COHEN] It's my pleasure to introduce our"},{"t":4.4,"txt":"first speaker."},{"t":5.3,"txt":"Ken Shotts is the David S. and Ann M."},{"t":7.6,"txt":"Barlow Professor of Political Economy at"},{"t":9.8,"txt":"the Stanford Graduate School of Business."},{"t":12.2,"txt":"He also teaches the core class Leading with Values."},{"t":16.1,"txt":"His research interests include electoral accountability and"},{"t":19.9,"txt":"policy entrepreneurship."},{"t":21.7,"txt":"And starting today, he is the new Vélez Reyes"},{"t":25.9,"txt":"Director of the Stanford Leadership Institute."},{"t":27.9,"txt":"Please join me in welcoming Ken Shotts."},{"t":36.8,"txt":"[KEN SHOTTS] Thank you, Maria."},{"t":38.3,"txt":"So hello and welcome to the Stanford Leadership Forum."},{"t":41.8,"txt":"So we're here at the Stanford Graduate School of Business."},{"t":45.7,"txt":"It's called the Graduate School of Business, but in some sense,"},{"t":49.5,"txt":"it's actually a school of leadership."},{"t":52.4,"txt":"And so is the rest of Stanford University,"},{"t":55.9,"txt":"a place where we educate and build leaders for the future."},{"t":60.4,"txt":"When I say the word leadership, I think for many people what"},{"t":63.4,"txt":"comes to mind is one's personal style, one's character,"},{"t":68.4,"txt":"how one runs or leads things within an organization."},{"t":72,"txt":"And those are obviously crucially important"},{"t":74.6,"txt":"components of leadership."},{"t":76.8,"txt":"But for people who take the mantle of leadership"},{"t":79.8,"txt":"and are in charge of big companies, governments,"},{"t":83.7,"txt":"and other organizations, leadership goes beyond that."},{"t":88.2,"txt":"And that's because we are at a time of rapid change,"},{"t":91.2,"txt":"and there are many complicated contextual forces that impact"},{"t":96.2,"txt":"firms and other organizations."},{"t":98.5,"txt":"This includes changes in science and technology, including AI."},{"t":102.7,"txt":"It includes questions about sustainability"},{"t":105,"txt":"and resource demands."},{"t":106.8,"txt":"It includes volatile markets, domestic political tensions,"},{"t":110,"txt":"geopolitical tensions, and cultural shifts"},{"t":113.2,"txt":"within countries."},{"t":115.5,"txt":"So how do we go about preparing leaders at a"},{"t":119.1,"txt":"time like this and at a place like Stanford University?"},{"t":123.7,"txt":"Well, we're a university, so we're obviously big believers"},{"t":126.9,"txt":"in scholarly knowledge."},{"t":128.1,"txt":"I mean, that's a big part of university, right?"},{"t":130.7,"txt":"But we are also big believers in the importance of having"},{"t":135.1,"txt":"people involved with deep practical experience"},{"t":140,"txt":"actually acting as leaders."},{"t":143.3,"txt":"We also want to be a place where"},{"t":145.7,"txt":"people throughout the community"},{"t":147.5,"txt":"jump in"},{"t":148.3,"txt":"and engage on important issues and challenges"},{"t":151,"txt":"that society faces."},{"t":152.6,"txt":"And that's not just because"},{"t":154,"txt":"those issues and challenges"},{"t":155.4,"txt":"are interesting and complicated"},{"t":156.8,"txt":"and important."},{"t":158.2,"txt":"It's also because those things"},{"t":159.8,"txt":"are crucial for"},{"t":160.8,"txt":"leadership as leadership."},{"t":163.7,"txt":"So we need leaders who have a deep understanding"},{"t":166.4,"txt":"of these contextual forces in society in the world."},{"t":170.5,"txt":"And we also need leaders who have a principled view that they"},{"t":175.3,"txt":"have developed on their own and thought through about their role"},{"t":180.2,"txt":"and the role of their company or organization in society."},{"t":184.3,"txt":"What are its responsibilities?"},{"t":186.1,"txt":"What things are not its responsibilities?"},{"t":188.4,"txt":"What are the responsibilities of other actors in society,"},{"t":191.5,"txt":"including governments?"},{"t":193.3,"txt":"The reason for this is leaders are not just people who react"},{"t":197.2,"txt":"to external forces in society."},{"t":199.6,"txt":"They also have agency to shape how those forces"},{"t":203.8,"txt":"impact their organizations and all of us in society."},{"t":208.4,"txt":"Now, to develop this knowledge and principled"},{"t":211.6,"txt":"sense of values requires hearing from, engaging with,"},{"t":215.1,"txt":"and learning from a lot of different people, including"},{"t":217.9,"txt":"people we disagree with."},{"t":219,"txt":"Often those are the most valuable sorts"},{"t":220.8,"txt":"of interactions to have are with people"},{"t":222.7,"txt":"who have a different perspective from our own."},{"t":225.1,"txt":"When we do that, we are better positioned"},{"t":227.8,"txt":"as leaders and as a society to make the sort of decisions"},{"t":233.1,"txt":"and build the sorts of institutions that we need"},{"t":236.1,"txt":"to face the challenges ahead."},{"t":238.9,"txt":"So that is why today I am delighted to announce the"},{"t":241.8,"txt":"official launch of the Stanford Leadership Institute."},{"t":245.2,"txt":"(applause)"},{"t":251.8,"txt":"[KEN SHOTTS] The mission of the Institute is to prepare leaders with"},{"t":254.8,"txt":"insights and strategies to navigate and shape our world,"},{"t":258.4,"txt":"improving how we do business and govern our society."},{"t":262.1,"txt":"To do this, we're establishing an"},{"t":264.1,"txt":"interdisciplinary hub for innovative research,"},{"t":265.9,"txt":"teaching, and convening."},{"t":267.7,"txt":"We're bringing together expertise from Stanford"},{"t":270.1,"txt":"and beyond to address the critical issues of our time"},{"t":273.4,"txt":"and to inspire leaders to make a positive impact in their"},{"t":277,"txt":"organizations and the world."},{"t":279.2,"txt":"So we've been building towards this day for"},{"t":281.4,"txt":"about five years now."},{"t":283,"txt":"The institute extends and expands the Business Governance"},{"t":286.6,"txt":"Society Initiative at the GSB"},{"t":288.8,"txt":"to create an institute that serves"},{"t":291.9,"txt":"all of Stanford University"},{"t":294.4,"txt":"The initiative has already funded over 100"},{"t":297.5,"txt":"research projects by over 60 different faculty members."},{"t":300.9,"txt":"We've introduced a bunch of things in the classroom,"},{"t":303.5,"txt":"including an Insights and Bites program where faculty come in"},{"t":307.1,"txt":"and share their cutting-edge research on current issues"},{"t":310.5,"txt":"of the day with students who want to learn from the faculty."},{"t":314.3,"txt":"We also have hosted a bunch of events and convenings,"},{"t":317.1,"txt":"including over 40 conferences on sustainability, a whole bunch"},{"t":321.1,"txt":"of events on technology and AI, including one you may have"},{"t":324.9,"txt":"heard about last week with Jensen Huang and Ro Khanna."},{"t":327.9,"txt":"So that was actually a Leadership Institute thing."},{"t":330.3,"txt":"And of course, the Stanford Leadership"},{"t":332.1,"txt":"Forum here today."},{"t":334.2,"txt":"The institute is based at the GSB and is going to"},{"t":337.4,"txt":"take the GSB's knowledge and extend it out to a"},{"t":340.5,"txt":"broader set of audiences."},{"t":342.3,"txt":"But it is also going to infuse stuff that goes on"},{"t":345.9,"txt":"within the business school with fresh insights from"},{"t":349.5,"txt":"others outside of the school and outside of the university."},{"t":352.6,"txt":"So it will improve the school and our depth"},{"t":355.3,"txt":"of knowledge as well."},{"t":357.1,"txt":"And I should also say, since this is Stanford, and"},{"t":359.7,"txt":"everything at Stanford needs an acronym or a nickname, right?"},{"t":363.4,"txt":"You think CoHo, SIEPR, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, CASBS."},{"t":366.4,"txt":"There's all sorts of acronyms around Stanford."},{"t":368.1,"txt":"So we need to be very clear about what the"},{"t":369.4,"txt":"right acronym is here."},{"t":370.7,"txt":"So the acronym for this thing is SLI for short, or the"},{"t":374.6,"txt":"Stanford Leadership Institute."},{"t":377.8,"txt":"So it's not SLE, right?"},{"t":378.8,"txt":"SLE is a program for undergrads."},{"t":380.8,"txt":"So it's something else completely different."},{"t":382.7,"txt":"Anyway, reaching this day has been a team effort across"},{"t":387.8,"txt":"the GSB and with colleagues around the university,"},{"t":390.9,"txt":"and I really appreciate the effort that many"},{"t":393,"txt":"people have put into this."},{"t":394.7,"txt":"I also want to take a moment to acknowledge the many donors"},{"t":398.7,"txt":"for the Leadership Institute who are in the room today."},{"t":401.9,"txt":"In particular, I want to thank the"},{"t":404,"txt":"foundational donors, Andreas and Diane Halvorsen."},{"t":407.9,"txt":"Your vision for the importance of leadership and the unique"},{"t":411.4,"txt":"opportunity for Stanford to shape our future has made"},{"t":415,"txt":"this institute possible."},{"t":416.9,"txt":"So thank you."},{"t":417.6,"txt":"(applause)"},{"t":421.5,"txt":"[SPEAKER 3] Thank you very much, Mr. President."},{"t":425.6,"txt":"[KEN SHOTTS] So today we're kicking off the Institute with"},{"t":427.6,"txt":"the Leadership Forum."},{"t":428.5,"txt":"Today we're going to have sessions on a whole bunch"},{"t":430,"txt":"of different topics."},{"t":431.6,"txt":"I'm guessing that each of you have particular sessions that"},{"t":434.3,"txt":"you're really excited to get to."},{"t":435.9,"txt":"You probably don't want to hear me talk too much longer, so I'm"},{"t":438.2,"txt":"not going to talk too much longer."},{"t":439.7,"txt":"But I do want to note that this forum is not just"},{"t":442.5,"txt":"about the conversations happening on the stage."},{"t":446,"txt":"It is also about fostering conversations amongst everyone"},{"t":449.6,"txt":"who is participating here, both today and into the"},{"t":453.4,"txt":"evening, and into the weeks and months, and years to come."},{"t":457,"txt":"Because that is what makes us, it possible for us to be better"},{"t":460.6,"txt":"leaders as we act and practice based on what we have learned."},{"t":464.9,"txt":"So, to get on today's first session,"},{"t":467.5,"txt":"it is my pleasure to introduce our first conversation with Dean"},{"t":470.7,"txt":"Sarah Sewell and former UK Prime Minister Rishi Sunak."},{"t":474.3,"txt":"(applause)"}],"words":[{"t":2.88,"w":"[MARIA"},{"t":2.88,"w":"COHEN]"},{"t":2.88,"w":"It's"},{"t":2.88,"w":"my"},{"t":2.88,"w":"pleasure"},{"t":2.88,"w":"to"},{"t":2.88,"w":"introduce"},{"t":2.88,"w":"our"},{"t":4.4,"w":"first"},{"t":4.4,"w":"speaker."},{"t":5.32,"w":"Ken"},{"t":5.32,"w":"Shotts"},{"t":5.32,"w":"is"},{"t":5.32,"w":"the"},{"t":5.32,"w":"David"},{"t":5.32,"w":"S."},{"t":5.32,"w":"and"},{"t":5.32,"w":"Ann"},{"t":5.32,"w":"M."},{"t":7.56,"w":"Barlow"},{"t":7.56,"w":"Professor"},{"t":7.56,"w":"of"},{"t":7.56,"w":"Political"},{"t":7.56,"w":"Economy"},{"t":7.56,"w":"at"},{"t":9.76,"w":"the"},{"t":9.76,"w":"Stanford"},{"t":9.76,"w":"Graduate"},{"t":9.76,"w":"School"},{"t":9.76,"w":"of"},{"t":9.76,"w":"Business."},{"t":12.2,"w":"He"},{"t":12.2,"w":"also"},{"t":12.2,"w":"teaches"},{"t":12.2,"w":"the"},{"t":12.2,"w":"core"},{"t":12.2,"w":"class"},{"t":12.2,"w":"Leading"},{"t":12.2,"w":"with"},{"t":12.2,"w":"Values."},{"t":16.12,"w":"His"},{"t":16.12,"w":"research"},{"t":16.12,"w":"interests"},{"t":16.12,"w":"include"},{"t":16.12,"w":"electoral"},{"t":16.12,"w":"accountability"},{"t":16.12,"w":"and"},{"t":19.88,"w":"policy"},{"t":19.88,"w":"entrepreneurship."},{"t":21.72,"w":"And"},{"t":21.72,"w":"starting"},{"t":21.72,"w":"today,"},{"t":21.72,"w":"he"},{"t":21.72,"w":"is"},{"t":21.72,"w":"the"},{"t":21.72,"w":"new"},{"t":21.72,"w":"Vélez"},{"t":21.72,"w":"Reyes"},{"t":25.92,"w":"Director"},{"t":25.92,"w":"of"},{"t":25.92,"w":"the"},{"t":25.92,"w":"Stanford"},{"t":25.92,"w":"Leadership"},{"t":25.92,"w":"Institute."},{"t":27.88,"